      }
    ],
    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "No, you can't. If a card is played at the same time as deletion by DP becoming 0, the [On Play] effect is triggered, but it can't activate because the card is deleted before it activates.",
        "question": "I played a Digimon with 5000 DP or less in a state where my opponent used this card's [When Digivolving][On Deletion] effect to give all of my Digimon -5000 DP. Can I activate my played Digimon's [On Play] effect before it's deleted by its DP becoming 0?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, you must activate it whenever possible.",
        "question": "Do I have to activate this card's [End of Attack] effect?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, it does.",
        "question": "Does this card's [End of Attack] effect also activate when my opponent has no Digimon in play?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      }
    ]
